rejected_labels:
Based on the given material, it appears that there has been no expression of interest from other NATO countries in taking over the mission in Oruzgan after August 2008. The Dutch government has requested Norway to take over the mission, but Norway has not expressed any interest in doing so. The survey conducted by De Vos & Jansen also suggests that the majority of the Dutch population does not support the mission and wants it to end, with only 45% of those polled supporting the mission and 45.6% supporting its extension beyond August 1, 2008. The main reason for the lack of support is the perception that the Dutch military are spending most of their time on war activities rather than rebuilding civil society, which was the original purpose of the mission. The Dutch government is expected to make a decision on a possible extension of the mission no later than September.<|im_end|>

